1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,147
Pairing two machines is easy.

2
00:00:01,147 --> 00:00:07,000
Knowing exactly what that pairing lets one do on the other is the part worth getting right — three switches, and a boundary that no switch can move.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,857
Three switches, all off by default.

4
00:00:08,857 --> 00:00:12,518
Models: let this device run inference using the remote's keys or GPU.

5
00:00:12,518 --> 00:00:14,588
Tools: let it call tools on the remote.

6
00:00:14,588 --> 00:00:17,878
Knowledge: let it search knowledge bases stored on the remote.

7
00:00:17,878 --> 00:00:20,000
Nothing is shared until you turn one on.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,701
Here's the boundary that doesn't move.

9
00:00:21,701 --> 00:00:26,716
Even with Tools switched on, shell, Python, and file-writing tools are never shared across the mesh — full stop.

10
00:00:26,716 --> 00:00:35,000
That's not a setting you can find and enable; it's a hard line in the design, because those three are exactly the tools that can do lasting damage to a machine that isn't yours to risk.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,676
For any paired device, What can it do?

12
00:00:37,676 --> 00:00:45,000
spells out exactly which switches are on and what that grants — no guessing from the toggle state alone.

13
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Turn Models on and the remote's models simply appear in your model picker alongside your local and cloud ones — same picker, no separate workflow.

14
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,026
If something's not connecting: check mesh is on at both ends, not just one.

15
00:00:56,026 --> 00:01:00,101
Discovery is a network broadcast that guest or corporate Wi-Fi often blocks — add by address instead.

16
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:04,176
The ports are 8793 for mesh traffic and 8794 for announcements, useful if you're touching a firewall.

17
00:01:04,176 --> 00:01:07,000
And a sleeping machine will correctly show offline — that's not a bug.

18
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:07,952
The mesh is covered.

19
00:01:07,952 --> 00:01:13,000
Now a different kind of portability — running this whole app with zero install, straight in a browser tab.

